<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juqu Wuhui</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 444</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juqu Wuhui was a prince of the Northern Liang dynasty in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juqu-mengxun">Juqu Mengxun</a>. After Northern Wei conquered the Northern Liang in 439, he and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juqu-anzhou">Juqu Anzhou</a> led the remnants of the family west, took Shanshan and in 442 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaochang">Gaochang</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turfan">Turpan</a>), where Wuhui ruled as king until his death in 444.</p></div>
